From 62f9a4f6417b7edd150065e5672d18d55b093e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lzc256 <i@lzc256.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:54:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add hold to talk on the message composer text input

Long pressing the text input of an empty composer now records a voice message:
the haptic feedback announces the recording, releasing the finger sends the
audio right away (without the preview step), and sliding the finger up by 60dp
switches to a cancel state (hinted with a pill) so that releasing discards the
recording. Recordings shorter than a second are considered accidental and are
discarded with a hint.

The gesture is implemented as a transparent overlay on top of the text input,
so it works for both the rich text and the legacy markdown editors, and it is
only composed while the composer is empty: as soon as some text is typed the
overlay is removed and long pressing behaves natively again. The gesture is
also disabled in edit, attachment and caption modes, when the voice permission
is not granted, and when the SC_HOLD_TO_TALK preference is turned off.
